  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For a fixed **binary** matrix BBB of size M×NM \\times NM×N, hErd calls a **binary** array AAA of size NNN lucky if:\n\n\n∑j=1NB(i,j)Aj≡0(mod2)\\displaystyle{\\sum_{j=1}^{N} B_{(i,j)} A_{j} \\equiv 0 \\pmod{2}}j=1∑N​B(i,j)​Aj​≡0(mod2)  for all 1≤i≤M1 \\leq i \\leq M1≤i≤M\nThe matrix BBB is constructed by setting B(i,j)&nbsp;(1≤i≤M,1≤j≤N)B_{(i,j)} \\ (1 \\leq i \\leq M,  1 \\leq j \\leq N)B(i,j)​&nbsp;(1≤i≤M,1≤j≤N) as 111 with probability p&nbsp;(0&lt;p≤1)p \\ (0 \\lt p \\leq 1)p&nbsp;(0&lt;p≤1). Note that input for ppp is given in format XY\\frac{X}{Y}YX​ where X≤YX \\leq YX≤Y.\n\nFor a positive integer sss, let EsE_{s}Es​ be the expected number of lucky arrays AAA such that ∑i=1NAi=s\\sum_{i=1}^{N} A_{i}=s∑i=1N​Ai​=s.\n\nGiven integer KKK, find the value ∑s=1KEs\\sum_{s=1}^{K} E_{s}∑s=1K​Es​.\n\nIt can be shown that the answer can be represented as PQ\\frac{P}{Q}QP​, where PPP and QQQ are coprime integers and Q≢0(mod109+7)Q \\not\\equiv 0 \\pmod{10^9+7}Q≡0(mod109+7). Print the value of P⋅Q−1(mod109+7)P \\cdot Q^{-1} \\pmod{10^9+7}P⋅Q−1(mod109+7).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nFirst and only line of each test contains 555 space-separated integers N,M,K,X,YN, M, K, X, YN,M,K,X,Y, as mentioned in the statement.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the value ∑s=1KEs\\sum_{s=1}^{K} E_{s}∑s=1K​Es​.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤M≤1051 \\leq M \\leq 10^51≤M≤105",
      "1≤K≤1051 \\leq K \\leq 10^51≤K≤105",
      "1≤X≤Y≤1091 \\leq X \\leq Y \\leq 10^91≤X≤Y≤109.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105.",
      "The sum of MMM over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105.",
      "The sum of KKK over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
